{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Should reps pick their name from a dropdown instead of typing it, so the log stays tidy?","Which call types and next steps match your sales process stages?","What lost reasons does your team actually hear, and would a new one reveal something worth tracking?","Does your team need the deal value on every call, or only once a proposal is sent?"],"howToUseResponses":"Review the log weekly in the dashboard, filtered by rep and outcome. Check that every live opportunity has a next step with a date, and chase any that slip past it. Count the lost reasons and the objections each month: if price keeps coming up, that is a pricing or positioning conversation, not a rep problem. Export to CSV when you need to merge the log with your pipeline.","customizeSteps":["Swap the call types, lost reasons and next steps for the stages and language your team already uses.","Turn the rep question into a dropdown of your team's names so every entry is spelled the same way.","Pin the link somewhere reps see it after every call, such as the team chat or a phone home screen."],"faqs":[{"q":"What should a sales call log include?","a":"Who was called and when, the type of call, the outcome, a short summary, objections, and the agreed next step with a date. Lost deals should record the reason."},{"q":"Why log sales calls in a form instead of a spreadsheet?","a":"A form asks the same questions every time and only the ones that fit the outcome, so entries stay consistent and reps actually finish them."},{"q":"Can I use this on my phone after a call?","a":"Yes. It runs as a chat, one question at a time, so it's easy to fill in on a phone. Most calls take a couple of minutes to log."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":9,"title":"Sales call log","description":"A quick log reps fill in after each call, with a next step every time.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_salescal00","ref":"welcome","title":"Just off a call? Log it now while it's fresh. Two minutes, tops.","required":false,"visi